target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckReadsTheRecordRatherThanBeingTold'
expect: a converged run must owe no disclosure
why:    `disclose: null` and `disclose: ""` are not the same answer to "what must the PR say". Step 14 reads this field, and an empty string is a disclosure that discloses nothing — indistinguishable, to anything checking for one, from a line that was rendered and lost.
--- old
	if disclose != "" {
		res.Disclose = &disclose
	}
--- new
	res.Disclose = &disclose
